{
  "fixture": "OTA open-loop DC-gain bench (issue #126): design/ota/ota_fd at the bias it has in the integrator's integrate phase (inputs at VCM = 0.9 V, outputs at the CMFB common mode, ibias 5 uA), differential gain read at the bottom of an ac sweep with the feedback loop open at ac and closed at dc",
  "source": "T",
  "result_kind": "simulated (ngspice, transistor-level netlist of design/ota/ota_fd; not the behavioural model). A simulated number is never called measured.",
  "model_b_parameter": "dc_gain (sim/bmodel/model.py), integrator amplifier DC gain A in V/V",
  "method": {
    "analysis": {
      "kind": "ac",
      "args": "dec 10 1 1000"
    },
    "why_ac_not_dc": "the open-loop operating point of a fully differential OTA is not stable, so there is no dc sweep to read; DR-001 item 2 names an ac response as the finite-gain method",
    "dc_asymptote": "reported at 1 Hz, the bottom of the sweep; the 1-1000 Hz band is gated flat to 0.01 relative per corner, which is what makes the reading a dc gain and not a band value",
    "loop_opening": "bench-only 1e12 H inductors carry the dc feedback (a short at dc, 6.3e12 ohm at 1 Hz against the ~1 Mohm output resistance) and 1 F capacitors carry the ac drive (open at dc, 0.16 ohm at 1 Hz)",
    "load": "1.8 pF per side, CL,eff inside the integrator per design/ota/SIZING.md. The dc gain does not depend on it; it is for comparability only.",
    "leaves_out": "gain-bandwidth, phase margin and the CMFB loop response (the settling bench and design/ota/SIZING.md own those); mismatch (this is the nominal grid, no Monte Carlo); and layout parasitics (DR-001 item 4, post-layout)"
  },
  "no_spec_budget": "spec/modulator-adc.md has no ratified DC-gain row: 5.3 budgets noise, not gain, so this record reports the per-corner value and its binding corner and makes no pass/fail against the spec. `pass` below is the reference-validity verdict of the three gates in make_request.py (drive magnitude, band flatness, common-mode rejection), not a spec verdict. design/ota/SIZING.md: whether ~55 dB is enough against the 80 dB target is a T-tier check, not decided there; issue #128 consumes these values into model B and answers it.",
  "conditions": {
    "vcm_V": 0.9,
    "ibias_uA": 5,
    "load_pF_per_side": 1.8,
    "ac_drive_V_differential": 1.0,
    "corner_set": "DR-002 full grid, 5 process x 3 T x 3 Vdda"
  },
